Q: ReactJS API Data Fetching CORS error A: <p>I was learning React and encountered this problem while using a custom hook to fetch JSON data from a remote server. If you have a local development environment (localhost) like me, and you want to resolve the problem quickly, your best bet is to use a CORS proxy server to modify the URL you wish to request before requesting with <code>fetch()</code> like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const sourceUrl = 'https://some.domain.com/resource.json';
const url = 'https://corsproxy.io/?' + encodeURIComponent(sourceUrl);

fetch(url)
    .then(response =&gt; response.json())
    .then(results =&gt; {
        return results;
    })
    .catch(error =&gt; {
        // handle error
    })
}
</code></pre>
<p><code>https://corsproxy.io/?</code> worked pretty well  as a proxy for me.</p>
<p>NOTE: This solution is not encouraged in production unless you own or trust the proxy server.</p>
